  "question": {
    "text": "The torque of a force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> about the origin is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#964;</mi></math>. If the force acts on a particle whose position vector is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#964;</mi></math> will be"
